        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "`pytest -V` no longer shows version; runs the full test session",
        "explanation": "A single '-V' (the documented alias of --version) is not caught by the early check in main(), which matches only the literal '--version'. Here config.option.version is 1, so the condition 'version > 1' is false. pytest_cmdline_main returns None and a normal test session runs instead of printing the version. The same happens to --version given through PYTEST_ADDOPTS or addopts; the changelog documents that case but not -V.",
        "suggestion": "When config.option.version == 1, write f\"pytest {pytest.__version__}\\n\" and return ExitCode.OK. Use show_version_verbose only when version > 1. Add a test for '-V'.",
        "evidence": "    if config.option.version > 1:",
        "confidence": 0.85,
        "id": "ddca4473d41c",
        "hunk_id": "src/_pytest/helpconfig.py#1",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "src/_pytest/config/__init__.py",
        "start_line": 153,
        "end_line": 156,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Early version check ignores -V alias; '-V --version' prints short form",
        "explanation": "The early exit counts only the literal string '--version'. The -V alias is ignored, so mixed forms go wrong: '-V --version' counts as two version flags in argparse, which before this change gave the verbose output, but the early check sees one '--version' and prints only the short version. A lone '-V' skips the early exit entirely and falls through to the plugin path, where it is mishandled (see helpconfig.py#1).",
        "suggestion": "Count both forms: n = sum(a in ('--version', '-V') for a in new_args) (or also handle combined forms such as '-VV'), and take the early exit only when n == 1.",
        "evidence": "if isinstance(new_args, Sequence) and new_args.count(\"--version\") == 1:",
        "confidence": 0.75,
        "id": "69b478ec16e6",
        "hunk_id": "src/_pytest/config/__init__.py#1",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "src/_pytest/config/__init__.py",
        "start_line": 1155,
        "end_line": 1160,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Usage-error path always shows verbose version, even for a single -V",
        "explanation": "The comment assumes only '--version --version' can reach this point. A single '-V', or --version coming from addopts, also reaches it when parsing fails. Those cases now print the verbose plugin listing instead of the short version.",
        "suggestion": "Keep the count check: call show_version_verbose only when self.option.version > 1; otherwise write the short 'pytest X' line.",
        "evidence": "show_version_verbose(self)",
        "confidence": 0.6,
